Feature: Filter list by tag

  Rule: Single tag filter
    Example: Shows yak with matching tag, hides others
    Example: Hides untagged yaks

  Rule: OR within a clause
    Example: Comma-separated tags match yaks with either tag
    Example: Yak with both tags also matches

  Rule: AND across clauses
    Example: Multiple --tag flags require yak to have all
    Example: Yak missing one required tag is hidden

  Rule: Combined AND/OR
    Example: --tag blocked,need-design --tag epic requires epic AND (blocked OR need-design)
    Example: Yak with epic but neither blocked nor need-design is hidden

  Rule: Ancestor context
    Example: Non-matching parent shown when child matches
    Example: Child of matching parent hidden if child doesn't match
    Example: Both shown when both match independently
    Example: Full ancestor chain shown for deeply nested match

  Rule: Combines with --only
    Example: --tag epic --only done shows only done yaks with epic tag
    Example: Ancestor context still applies with combined filters

  Rule: Tag normalization
    Example: --tag @epic treated same as --tag epic
    Example: --tag @foo,@bar strips @ from all values

  Rule: No matches
    Example: Empty result when no yaks have the tag
    Example: JSON format returns empty array
